# 13. Why NumPy is Fast

Python List:

* Stores references.
* Different data types allowed.

NumPy Array:

* Stores same datatype.
* Continuous memory allocation.
* Vectorized operations.

Result:

```text
Faster computation
Lower memory usage
Better mathematical operations
```

